{
  "sources": [
    {
      "id": "src-fastned-tesla-curves-2026",
      "type": "testing_org",
      "title": "Fastned: Tesla Model 3 charge curves (Long Range 2019-2023, Standard Range 2020-2023)",
      "url": "https://www.fastnedcharging.com/en/brands-overview/tesla",
      "accessed_on": "2026-11-19",
      "notes": "Fastned publishes per-car charge curves measured on its own European CCS2 network (300 kW chargers); the numbers are embedded in the page (kW at each whole SoC %). Page says curves show behaviour with a battery at about 30 C; colder/warmer packs charge slower. CCS2, not Tesla Supercharger, so the peak is capped below the car's Supercharger peak. Fastned Terms of Use (en-gb terms-conditions) are readable and have no clause on reuse of site data; robots.txt allows crawling; no licence for the charge graphs either way, so the owner confirms."
    },
    {
      "id": "src-fastned-tesla-model-y-2026",
      "type": "testing_org",
      "title": "Fastned: Tesla Model Y Long Range (2022 - 2025) charge curve",
      "url": "https://www.fastnedcharging.com/en/brands-overview/tesla?model=Model%20Y",
      "accessed_on": "2026-11-19",
      "notes": "Same Fastned Tesla page family, Model Y filter. Curve measured on Fastned's European CCS2 network, battery about 30 C, chargeSpeed 250 kW, graph class 300 kW. Terms as for src-fastned-tesla-curves-2026 (no reuse clause in the readable Terms of Use). The \"Long Range (2025+)\" entry carries identical numbers (checked all 82 points), so it adds no second measurement. The Model Y \"Standard Range\" entries (2022-2025, 2025+) have no graph."
    }
  ],
